               has enabled analyses of over 10,000 families, supporting the
               diagnosis of more than 3,800 individuals with rare disease and
               discovery of over 300 novel disease genes. Here, we describe a
               framework for genomic analysis in rare disease that leverages
               seqr's capabilities for variant filtration, annotation, and
               causal variant identification, as well as support for research
